IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `er5-pilot-hours`

-- Tests of er5-pilot-hours (reg 77.994). Expected values are written by hand from the text of the Regulations (SOR-96-332.txt lines 1599-1609),
-- beside each assertion, before the run. The text never states the day on which reg 77.994 comes into force; the tests use October 1, 2024, an invented day.

§ `Reg 77.994(1) - purposes (src:1599-1601)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.994(1)(a) the first purpose of Pilot Project No. 23` EQUALS "the effectiveness of a one-time credit of additional hours of insurable employment in mitigating the impact of evacuations due to natural disasters on the benefits payable to claimants under Part I of the Act"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(1)(b) the second purpose of Pilot Project No. 23` EQUALS "the effectiveness of using postal codes to identify the claimants to whom that credit should apply"

§ `Reg 77.994(2) - the postal codes (src:1602)`

-- The argument order is: the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I; the postal code of the area where the claimant is ordinarily resident.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` TRUE "T0E 1E0"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` TRUE "T0E 0C0"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` TRUE "R0B 1C0"
-- A neighbouring code; the same code written without its space or in lower case (not the string the text writes).
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` TRUE "T0E 1E1")
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` TRUE "T0E1E0")
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` TRUE "t0e 1e0")
-- Not an initial claim under Part I.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2) the claimant makes an initial claim under Part I while ordinarily resident in an area with one of the postal codes` FALSE "T0E 1E0")

§ `Reg 77.994(2)(a) - a benefit period already established (src:1603)`

-- The argument order is: the base condition; a benefit period is established in respect of the claim; the day it begins; the day it ended under paragraph 10(8)(d), if it did; the day the section comes into force.
-- A benefit period beginning on Sunday July 21, 2024, the first day allowed.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 7 21) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 1)
-- The day before: too early.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 7 20) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 1))
-- September 30, 2024, the day before the section comes into force: allowed. The day it comes into force: not (that is paragraph (b)'s).
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 9 30) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 10 1) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 1))
-- Ended under paragraph 10(8)(d) on September 30, 2024, before the section came into force: out. Ended on the day it came into force: not "before" it, so in.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 8 4) (JUST (YMD 2024 9 30)) (YMD 2024 10 1))
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE TRUE (YMD 2024 8 4) (JUST (YMD 2024 10 1)) (YMD 2024 10 1)
-- No benefit period established; the base condition not met.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` TRUE FALSE (YMD 2024 8 4) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(a) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(a)` FALSE TRUE (YMD 2024 8 4) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 1))

§ `Reg 77.994(2)(b) - a claim made in the window (src:1604)`

-- The argument order is: the base condition; the day the claim is made; the day the section comes into force.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` TRUE (YMD 2024 10 1) (YMD 2024 10 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` TRUE (YMD 2024 9 30) (YMD 2024 10 1))
-- Saturday July 19, 2025, the last day; the day after.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` TRUE (YMD 2025 7 19) (YMD 2024 10 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` TRUE (YMD 2025 7 20) (YMD 2024 10 1))
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(2)(b) the claimant is referred to in paragraph (2)(b)` FALSE (YMD 2025 1 1) (YMD 2024 10 1))

§ `Reg 77.994(3) and (4) - the additional 300 hours (src:1605-1608)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.994(3) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have` TRUE EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(3) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have` FALSE EQUALS 0
-- The argument order of (4) is: referred to in (2)(b); a benefit period was established for a previous claim referred to in (2)(b); a previous claim with a benefit period referred to in (2)(a).
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have in relation to the claim` TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have in relation to the claim` TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have in relation to the claim` TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have in relation to the claim` FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0

§ `Reg 77.994(5) - what the hours count for (src:1609)`

#ASSERT `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "subsection 28(4) of the Act"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "paragraph 30(1)(a) of the Act"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "paragraph 31(c) of the Act"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "paragraph 32(2)(c) of the Act"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "subsection 35(3) of the Regulations"
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "subparagraph 35(7)(e)(ii) of the Regulations"
-- Section 7 of the Act (the hours required to qualify) is not on the list: the text does not name it.
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` TRUE "section 7 of the Act")
#ASSERT NOT (`reg 77.994(5) the additional hours are also considered hours of insurable employment for the purposes of the provision` FALSE "subsection 28(4) of the Act")

§ `Reg 77.994(2) to (4) as a whole (src:1602-1608)`

-- The argument order is: an initial claim under Part I; the postal code; a benefit period is established for the claim; the day it begins; the day it ended under 10(8)(d), if it did; the day the claim is made;
-- the day the section comes into force (October 1, 2024, invented); a benefit period established for a previous claim under (2)(b); a previous claim with a benefit period of (2)(a).
-- A benefit period beginning on August 4, 2024 and still running when the section comes into force: referred to in (2)(a); 300 hours.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` TRUE "T0E 1E0" TRUE (YMD 2024 8 4) NOTHING (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2024 10 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 300
-- A claim made on October 15, 2024, after the section comes into force, with its benefit period beginning October 20, 2024: referred to in (2)(b); 300 hours.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` TRUE "R0B 1C0" TRUE (YMD 2024 10 20) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 15) (YMD 2024 10 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 300
-- The same claim, but the claimant already had a benefit period of paragraph (2)(a) for a previous claim: (4)(b) takes the hours away.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` TRUE "R0B 1C0" TRUE (YMD 2024 10 20) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 15) (YMD 2024 10 1) FALSE TRUE EQUALS 0
-- ... or a benefit period established for a previous claim referred to in (2)(b): (4)(a) takes them away.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` TRUE "R0B 1C0" TRUE (YMD 2024 10 20) NOTHING (YMD 2024 10 15) (YMD 2024 10 1) TRUE FALSE EQUALS 0
-- A postal code outside the list; a claim made after July 19, 2025.
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` TRUE "T0E 1E1" TRUE (YMD 2024 8 4) NOTHING (YMD 2024 8 1) (YMD 2024 10 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
#ASSERT `reg 77.994(2) to (4) the additional hours of insurable employment that the claimant is deemed to have for the claim` TRUE "T0E 1E0" TRUE (YMD 2025 7 21) NOTHING (YMD 2025 7 20) (YMD 2024 10 1) FALSE FALSE EQUALS 0
